==================================================
ROB INDEXING RULE
==================================================
Factory event:
TokenLaunched
provides the new:
TOKEN
CURVE
DEPLOYER
PAIR
LAUNCH CONFIG
GRADUATION THRESHOLD.
ROB then begins indexing that individual curve.
==================================================
CURVE BUY SEMANTICS
==================================================
CurveBuy contains:
buyer
recipient
quoteIn
tokensOut
fee
tax
For research interpretation:
tax
is creator tax.
fee
contains the base trade fee.
For a qualifying opening-window buy, the opening snipe-tax component is folded into:
fee.
Therefore the raw event does not directly provide:
snipeTax
as a separate field.
ROB must calculate that component only when the required base-fee state is known.
==================================================
CURVE SELL SEMANTICS
==================================================
CurveSell contains:
seller
recipient
tokensIn
quoteOut
fee
tax
ROB preserves the event exactly before performing derived calculations.
==================================================
ROB RAW EVENT FIRST
==================================================
For each event:
1. Preserve raw log.
2. Preserve transaction hash.
3. Preserve block number.
4. Preserve block hash.
5. Preserve transaction index.
6. Preserve log index.
7. Decode event.
8. Link experiment.
9. Calculate timing.
10. Calculate fee components.
11. Classify behavior.
12. Preserve method version.
==================================================
OPENING FEE CALCULATION
==================================================
Conceptually:
INFERRED_OPENING_FEE
=
EVENT FEE
-
ORDINARY BASE TRADE FEE
when protocol semantics and units support the subtraction.
Creator tax is already reported separately as:
tax.
If the ordinary fee cannot be established:
return:
UNKNOWN.
